[0.007661,"o","\u001b[?1049h\u001b[24;1H\u001b[?1h\r"]
[0.008794,"o","\u001b[4mDNF4.CONF\u001b[24m(5)                                             DNF                                             \u001b[4mDNF4.CONF\u001b[24m(5)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m"]
[0.000123,"o","\r\n\u001b[1mNAME\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       dnf4.conf - DNF Configuration Reference\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[4mDNF\u001b[24m  by  default  uses  the  global  configuration  file at \u001b[1m/etc/dnf/dnf.conf \u001b[22mand all *.repo files found under\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1m/etc/yum.repos.d\u001b[22m. The latter is typically used for repository configuration and takes precedence  over  global\u001b[m\r\n       configuration.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       The  configuration  file has INI format consisting of section declaration and \u001b[1mname=value \u001b[22moptions below each on\u001b[m\r\n       separate line. There are two types of sections in the configuration files: main and repository.  Main  section\u001b[m\r\n       defines all global configuration options and should be only one.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       The  repository  sections  define the configuration for each (remote or local) repository. The section name of\u001b[m\r\n       the repository in brackets serve as repo ID reference and should be unique across configuration files. The al‐\u001b[m\r\n       lowed characters of repo ID string are lower and upper case alphabetic letters, digits, \u001b[1m-\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m_\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m.   \u001b[22mand  \u001b[1m:\u001b[22m.  The\u001b[m\r\n       minimal  repository  configuration  file should aside from repo ID consists of \u001b[4mbaseurl\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mmetalink\u001b[24m or \u001b[4mmirrorlist\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       option definition.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mDISTRIBUTION-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       Configuration options, namely \u001b[4mbest\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mskip_if_unavailable\u001b[24m, can be set in the DNF configuration file  by  your\u001b[m\r\n       distribution to override the DNF defaults.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page dnf.conf(5) line 1 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.010406,"o","\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1m[MAIN] OPTIONS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1mallow_vendor_change\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              If disabled dnf will stick to vendor when upgrading or downgrading rpms.  Default is \u001b[1mTrue\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[1mWARNING:\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n                 This option is currently not supported for \u001b[4mdowngrade\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mdistro-sync\u001b[24m commands\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m"]
[0.000076,"o","\r\n       \u001b[1march   \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              The  architecture  used  for installing packages. By default this is auto-detected. Often used together\u001b[m\r\n              with \u001b[4mignorearch\u001b[24m option.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1massumeno\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              If enabled dnf will assume \u001b[1mNo \u001b[22mwhere it would normally prompt for confirmation from user input.  Default\u001b[m\r\n              is \u001b[1mFalse\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1massumeyes\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page dnf.conf(5) line 24 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[3.039945,"o","\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n              If  enabled  dnf  will  assume \u001b[1mYes \u001b[22mwhere it would normally prompt for confirmation from user input (see\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.000399,"o","              also \u001b[4mdefaultyes\u001b[24m). Default is \u001b[1mFalse\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1mautocheck_running_kernel\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              Automatic check whether there is installed newer kernel module with security update than currently run‐\u001b[m\r\n              ning kernel. Default is \u001b[1mTrue\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1mbasearch\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              The base architecture used for installing packages. By default this is auto-detected.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1mbest   \u001b[4m\u001b[22mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[1mTrue \u001b[22minstructs the solver to either use a package with the highest available version or fail. On \u001b[1mFalse\u001b[22m,\u001b[m\r\n              do not fail if the latest version cannot be installed and go with the lower  version.  The  default  is\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[1mFalse\u001b[22m.  Note this option in particular \u001b[4mcan\u001b[24m \u001b[4mbe\u001b[24m \u001b[4mset\u001b[24m \u001b[4min\u001b[24m \u001b[4myour\u001b[24m \u001b[4mconfiguration\u001b[24m \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m \u001b[4mby\u001b[24m \u001b[4myour\u001b[24m \u001b[4mdistribution\u001b[24m. Also\u001b[m\r\n              note  that  the  use  of the highest available version is only guaranteed for the packages directly re‐\u001b[m\r\n              quested and not for their dependencies.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page dnf.conf(5) line 47 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[3.017414,"o","\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              \u001b[4mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1massumeyes\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM              is \u001b[1mFalse\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM              If enabled dnf will assume \u001b[1mNo \u001b[22mwhere it would normally prompt for confirmation from user input.  Default\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.000009,"o","\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM              \u001b[4mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1massumeno\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM              with \u001b[4mignorearch\u001b[24m option.\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.000015,"o","\u001b[H\u001bM              The  architecture  used  for installing packages. By default this is auto-detected. Often used together\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1march   \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                 This option is currently not supported for \u001b[4mdowngrade\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mdistro-sync\u001b[24m commands\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM              \u001b[1mWARNING:\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.000022,"o","\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM              If disabled dnf will stick to vendor when upgrading or downgrading rpms.  Default is \u001b[1mTrue\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM              \u001b[4mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mallow_vendor_change\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[1m[MAIN] OPTIONS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[24;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page dnf.conf(5) line 24 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
