[0.009697,"o","\u001b[4mDNF4.CONF\u001b[24m(5)                                             DNF                                             \u001b[4mDNF4.CONF\u001b[24m(5)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mNAME\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       dnf4.conf - DNF Configuration Reference\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m"]
[0.000009,"o","\r\n"]
[0.000021,"o","\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.000022,"o","       \u001b[4mDNF\u001b[24m  by  default  uses  the  global  configuration  file at \u001b[1m/etc/dnf/dnf.conf \u001b[22mand all *.repo files found under\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.000021,"o","       \u001b[1m/etc/yum.repos.d\u001b[22m. The latter is typically used for repository configuration and takes precedence  over  global\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.000012,"o","       configuration.\u001b[m\r\n"]
[0.000165,"o","\u001b[m\r\n       The  configuration  file has INI format consisting of section declaration and \u001b[1mname=value \u001b[22moptions below each on\u001b[m\r\n       separate line. There are two types of sections in the configuration files: main and repository.  Main  section\u001b[m\r\n       defines all global configuration options and should be only one.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       The  repository  sections  define the configuration for each (remote or local) repository. The section name of\u001b[m\r\n       the repository in brackets serve as repo ID reference and should be unique across configuration files. The al‐\u001b[m\r\n       lowed characters of repo ID string are lower and upper case alphabetic letters, digits, \u001b[1m-\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m_\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m.   \u001b[22mand  \u001b[1m:\u001b[22m.  The\u001b[m\r\n       minimal  repository  configuration  file should aside from repo ID consists of \u001b[4mbaseurl\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mmetalink\u001b[24m or \u001b[4mmirrorlist\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       option definition.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mDISTRIBUTION-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       Configuration options, namely \u001b[4mbest\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mskip_if_unavailable\u001b[24m, can be set in the DNF configuration file  by  your\u001b[m\r\n       distribution to override the DNF defaults.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page dnf.conf(5) line 1 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[3.002076,"o","\r\u001b[K/\u001b[Ki\bi\u001b[Kn\bn\u001b[Ks\bs\u001b[Kt\bt\u001b[Ka\ba\u001b[Kl\bl\u001b[Kl\bl\u001b[Ko\bo\u001b[Kn\bn\u001b[Kl\bl\u001b[Ky\by\u001b[K_\b_\u001b[Kl\bl\u001b[Ki\bi\u001b[Km\bm\u001b[Ki\bi"]
[0.000132,"o","\u001b[Kt\bt"]
[3.035759,"o","\r\u001b[K"]
[0.000253,"o","\u001b[1;1H\u001b[K\u001b[4mDNF4.CONF\u001b[24m(5)                                             DNF                                             \u001b[4mDNF4.CONF\u001b[24m(5)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[2;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[3;1H\u001b[K\u001b[1mNAME\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4;1H\u001b[K       dnf4.conf - DNF Configuration Reference\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[5;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6;1H\u001b[K\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7;1H\u001b[K       \u001b[4mDNF\u001b[24m  by  default  uses  the  global  configuration  file at \u001b[1m/etc/dnf/dnf.conf \u001b[22mand all *.repo files found under\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[8;1H\u001b[K       \u001b[1m/etc/yum.repos.d\u001b[22m. The latter is typically used for repository configuration and takes precedence  over  global\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[9;1H\u001b[K       configuration.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[10;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[11;1H\u001b[K       The  configuration  file has INI format consisting of section declaration and \u001b[1mname=value \u001b[22moptions below each on\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[12;1H\u001b[K       separate line. There are two types of sections in the configuration files: main and repository.  Main  section\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[13;1H\u001b[K       defines all global configuration options and should be only one.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[14;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[15;1H\u001b[K       The  repository  sections  define the configuration for each (remote or local) repository. The section name of\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[16;1H\u001b[K       the repository in brackets serve as repo ID reference and should be unique across configuration files. The al‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[17;1H\u001b[K       lowed characters of repo ID string are lower and upper case alphabetic letters, digits, \u001b[1m-\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m_\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m.   \u001b[22mand  \u001b[1m:\u001b[22m.  The\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[18;1H\u001b[K       minimal  repository  configuration  file should aside from repo ID consists of \u001b[4mbaseurl\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mmetalink\u001b[24m or \u001b[4mmirrorlist\u001b[0m\u001b[m"]
[0.000013,"o","\r\n"]
[0.000016,"o","\u001b[19;1H\u001b[K       option definition.\u001b[m"]
[0.000385,"o","\r\n\u001b[20;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[21;1H\u001b[K\u001b[1mDISTRIBUTION-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[22;1H\u001b[K       Configuration options, namely \u001b[4mbest\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mskip_if_unavailable\u001b[24m, can be set in the DNF configuration file  by  your\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[23;1H\u001b[K       distribution to override the DNF defaults.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[24;1H\u001b[1;1H\u001b[K\u001b[4mDNF4.CONF\u001b[24m(5)                                             DNF                                             \u001b[4mDNF4.CONF\u001b[24m(5)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[2;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[3;1H\u001b[K\u001b[1mNAME\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4;1H\u001b[K       dnf4.conf - DNF Configuration Reference\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[5;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6;1H\u001b[K\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7;1H\u001b[K       \u001b[4mDNF\u001b[24m  by  default  uses  the  global  configuration  file at \u001b[1m/etc/dnf/dnf.conf \u001b[22mand all *.repo files found under\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[8;1H\u001b[K       \u001b[1m/etc/yum.repos.d\u001b[22m. The latter is typically used for repository configuration and takes precedence  over  global\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[9;1H\u001b[K       configuration.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[10;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[11;1H\u001b[K       The  configuration  file has INI format consisting of section declaration and \u001b[1mname=value \u001b[22moptions below each on\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[12;1H\u001b[K       separate line. There are two types of sections in the configuration files: main and repository.  Main  section\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[13;1H\u001b[K       defines all global configuration options and should be only one.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[14;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[15;1H\u001b[K       The  repository  sections  define the configuration for each (remote or local) repository. The section name of\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[16;1H\u001b[K       the repository in brackets serve as repo ID reference and should be unique across configuration files. The al‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[17;1H\u001b[K       lowed characters of repo ID string are lower and upper case alphabetic letters, digits, \u001b[1m-\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m_\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m.   \u001b[22mand  \u001b[1m:\u001b[22m.  The\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[18;1H\u001b[K       minimal  repository  configuration  file should aside from repo ID consists of \u001b[4mbaseurl\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mmetalink\u001b[24m or \u001b[4mmirrorlist\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[19;1H\u001b[K       option definition.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[20;1H\u001b[K\u001b[m"]
[0.000127,"o","\r\n\u001b[21;1H\u001b[K\u001b[1mDISTRIBUTION-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[22;1H\u001b[K       Configuration options, namely \u001b[4mbest\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mskip_if_unavailable\u001b[24m, can be set in the DNF configuration file  by  your\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[23;1H\u001b[K       distribution to override the DNF defaults.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[24;1H"]
[0.000178,"o","...skipping...\r\n"]
[0.000114,"o","              sions is regulated by \u001b[4m\u001b[7minstallonly_limit\u001b[27m\u001b[4m\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1m\u001b[7minstallonly_limit\u001b[27m\u001b[1m\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4minteger\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              Number  of \u001b[4minstallonly\u001b[24m \u001b[4mpackages\u001b[24m allowed to be installed concurrently. Defaults to 3. The minimal number\u001b[m\r\n              of installonly packages is 2. Value 0 means unlimited number of installonly packages. Value  1  is  ex‐\u001b[m\r\n              plicitly  not allowed since it complicates kernel upgrades due to protection of the running kernel from\u001b[m\r\n              removal.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1minstallroot\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              The root of the filesystem for all packaging  operations.  It  requires  an  absolute  path.  See  also\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4m--installroot\u001b[24m \u001b[4mcommandline\u001b[24m \u001b[4moption\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1minstall_weak_deps\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n              When this option is set to True and a new package is about to be installed, all packages linked by weak\u001b[m\r\n              dependency  relation (Recommends or Supplements flags) with this package will be pulled into the trans‐\u001b[m\r\n              action.  Default is \u001b[1mTrue\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page dnf.conf(5) line 185 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.037313,"o","\r\u001b[K/\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1mkeepcache\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n              \u001b[4mboolean\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page dnf.conf(5) line 187 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
